        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "The Barman Cloud plugin (0.15.x) exports exactly three gauges - `last_available_backup_timestamp`, `last_failed_backup_timestamp` and `first_recoverability_point` - on the instance manager. There is **no** metric for base-backup size, duration, throughput or per-backup status, and the in-core `cnpg_collector_last_*_backup_timestamp` gauges are deprecated and permanently 0 on this cluster.\n\nSo for size and history, use the API objects and the bucket:\n\n```\nkubectl -n cloudnative-pg get backups \\\n  -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,PHASE:.status.phase,STARTED:.status.startedAt,STOPPED:.status.stoppedAt\n```\n\nA backup that failed on its first attempt and succeeded on retry will still read as `completed` here, and the archive size lives in B2. `cnpg_pg_stat_archiver_failed_count` is the only failure signal on the WAL side, and it is cumulative since stats reset.",
